  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nThe track of the center of Hurricane Marie is expected to be\ntoward the west northwest through Saturday. For Saturday evening,\nthat would place it well to the south of Point Conception and \nwell to the west and a little to the south of the southern tip of \nBaja.\n\nChances for showers will increase on Sunday along with a slight\nchance of thunderstorms on Sunday afternoon for the mountains,\ndeserts, and inland valleys. Chance for showers will then decrease\nfor Sunday night and Labor Day. There is greater spread in the\nhigh temperature guidance on Sunday due to differences in the\namount of moisture influx and clouds. \n\nThere is a 40 to 50 percent chance of one-tenth inch or more of\nrainfall for lower elevations with chances for one inch or more \nof rainfall in the mountains of 10 to 20 percent.\n\nSurf from Hurricane Marie is expected to increase on Saturday and\nSaturday night, peak on Sunday and Sunday night, then begin to\nslowly diminish on Labor Day.",
